                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On February 14 and 23, Assistant Secretary Rusk discussed United States policy
                    with regard to China with Canadian Ambassador Hume <pb facs="0121" n="1579"
                        xml:id="pg1579"/> Wrong. No record of either conversation has been found in
                    the Department of State files; Wrong’s reports of the conversations, sent in
                    personal letters to Canadian Secretary of State for External Affairs Lester B.
                    Pearson, are quoted in part in <hi rendition="#italic">Mike: The Memoirs of the
                        Right Honourable Lester B. Pearson</hi>, Volume 2: 1948–1957, edited by John
                    A. Munro and Alex I. Inglis (Toronto: University of Toronto Press, 1973), pages
                    175–179.</p>
            </div>
